+# Act 23 §7: pre-cutover open-case register (current-main additive candidate)
+
+This register is a **durable obligation inventory**, not independent verification
+of case closure and not evidence that any old report is endorsed. The source of
+truth for live case state remains the original `viche-state` case JSON and
+terminal evidence; an absent or stale snapshot is an investigation target, not
+proof that no obligation remains.
+
+The three cases below were recorded as open in the reviewed October cutover
+snapshot (2026-10-30T17:08Z). They must be re-read from live state before any
+closure claim; no agent exit, clean process state, board comment or archive/move
+operation closes them.
+
+| Case ID | Repair owner | Evidence required | Independent verifier and gate |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `continuity_unverified_c1a00001:1793180537` | Executive (Clerk for parliamentary seat) | Original case JSON, terminal agent logs, external-effect reconciliation, tested successor handoff | Judiciary must independently verify before closure |
+| `continuity_unverified_executive:1793236881` | Executive (Clerk for parliamentary seat) | Original case JSON, terminal agent logs, external-effect reconciliation, tested successor handoff | Judiciary must independently verify before closure |
+| `continuity_unverified_judiciary:1793190195` | Executive (Clerk for parliamentary seat) | Original case JSON, terminal agent logs, external-effect reconciliation, tested successor handoff | Judiciary must independently verify before closure |
+
+Act 23 §5.1 independent closure gate: no obligation or case may be closed
+without evidence-backed verification by an independent office (Clerk or
+Judiciary as specified by the duty). A journal entry, process exit, "running"
+or "stopped" status, a passing test, a commit or a board comment is never
+closure. Cases discovered during transition must be inventoried here with a
+named owner, required evidence, independent verifier and closure gate.
+
+This candidate does not close, rename, archive or replay any of these cases.
