+# Act 23 §4.1: mandatory operational duty mapping (current-main additive candidate)
+
+This file is a **proposed cutover gate**, NOT evidence that any old case is
+resolved, and NOT a licence to delete any current mechanism. Each entry must be
+independently checked against the law that created the duty.
+
+Canonical base for this candidate: `origin/main` @ `1d3a949c` (2026-11-24).
+Act 23 (`agentic-operations-act`, enacted 2026-10-29T17:12Z, bill digest
+`356fdfbb…`, six affirmative ballots, `tally.sh` PASSED) is enacted ordinary
+law. The deletion-oriented implementation reviewed as PR #45 was built on the
+October main (`3e1855e8`) and predates Acts 25, 27, 30, 31, 32 and 34. This
+candidate therefore implements Act 23 **additively**: it introduces the
+agent-owned responsibility substrate and maps every duty, but retains every
+ mechanism that a later enacted Act still requires. Deletion of any retained
+mechanism below requires an express repeal/replacement enacted by Parliament;
+an Executive candidate cannot supply it.
+
+## Retired-or-reassigned mechanisms and their duty mapping
+
+| Retired/reassigned mechanism and statutory duty | Accountable owner | Durable evidence required | Independent verifier | Pass/fail criterion and gate |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Act 15: `audit-cycle.sh` randomized investigation | Judiciary | `audit-selection.py` selection provenance and Git-anchored `records/AUDIT` evidence | Clerk and non-reviewed parliamentary member | Bounded independent sampled review in each legal window; unsupported green status fails |
+| Act 15: `branch-liveness.sh` and `branch-health.sh` | Executive continuity; Judiciary inquiry | original Antonina invocation status, logs, independent `oversight-watch.sh` evidence, office journal | Judiciary | Every interruption remains visible and recoverable until independent review |
+| Act 17: `institutional-cases.py` corrective case generation and verification | Executive repair; Judiciary verification | original `viche-state/institutional-cases/index.json` and case JSON, append-only correction trail | Judiciary separate from repairer | No case closure absent independently checked original terminal effects |
+| Act 17: correction-integrity audit | Judiciary | `records/AUDIT` and `audit-accountability.py` outputs | Clerk or other independent parliamentary member | No prior correction described as operative without legal evidence |
+| Act 18: `outcome-metrics.py` and scripted board delivery summary | Clerk reporting, Executive substantiation | `board-trail-refresh.sh` generated complete index, board records, Town Hall 302 messages, verified work artifacts | Judiciary | Correct sourced changes in statutory reporting window, not commit or agent-count proxies |
+| Act 19: `branch-bootstrap.sh`, office-specific cycles, seat continuity | Clerk for seats; Executive for officers; Recovery Steward for incapacitated agents | `records/handoffs`, `handoff-queue.sh`, historical appointment and terminal logs, `office-blockers` receipts | Judiciary | Terminal or running writers cannot replay, blockers are Clerk-visible; successor verifies external effects |
+| Act 19: `office-continuity.sh` scripted reset | Recovery Steward | terminal invocation evidence, replacement appointment, continuity journal | Judiciary | Open obligations survive arbitrary failure, no duplicate side effect, independent verification |
+| Act 21: exact-commit quality gate | Clerk | exact commit SHA/tree, clean isolated worktree `tests/run-all.sh`, independent review and CI | Judiciary for statutory review | No merge/deploy on absent exact-commit test, reviewer, clean status, or verified evidence |
+| Act 23: old case inventory and closure | Executive repairs, Judiciary verifies | `records/agentic-cutover-open-cases.md` and original `viche-state` case JSON | Judiciary | Named owner and evidence for every open case, no silent closure on process exit |
+
+Mechanical identity, permission, physical-resource, audit integrity, tally,
+board index and oversight tools remain when required. Agent reasoning owns
+open-ended decisions, not shell-based process success heuristics.
+
+## Mechanisms that MUST be retained on current main (later enacted law)
+
+The October deletion patch deletes the following files. Each is still present
+on `origin/main` and is required by law enacted **after** Act 23. Deleting any
+of them would breach current law; they are therefore explicitly retained in
+this candidate.
+
+| Mechanism the old patch deletes | Current enacted duty that forbids deletion | Disposition in this candidate |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `government/audit-cycle.sh`, `tests/audit-cycle-identity-smoke.sh`, `tests/randomized-audit-smoke.sh` | Act 27 §1 (enacted 2026-11-08) makes the cycle token from the audit dispatch authoritative and records it in `state/audit-cycle-identities.tsv`; Act 15 independent randomized audit preserved by Act 23 §4 and Act 34 §7 | Retained |
+| `government/executive-innovation-cycle.sh` | Act 25 §3 (re-enacted 2026-11-08) expressly authorizes activation of the "already-reviewed dormant" script | Retained |
+| `government/branch-health.sh`, `government/branch-liveness.sh` | Act 25 §3 requires schema/writer updates to `branch-health.sh` and branch liveness to track the new authority | Retained |
+| `government/innovation-centre-cycle.sh` | Act 25 §§1–5 preserve appointment key `innovation-centre`, worktree and dispatch continuity through transfer | Retained |
+| `government/oversight-watch.sh`, `tests/oversight-smoke.sh`, `tests/oversight-release-signal-smoke.sh` | Act 23 §3 names reliable evidence capture and independent oversight; Act 34 §7 preserves Act 15 independent methods | Retained |
+| `government/institutional-cases.py`, `tests/institutional-recovery-smoke.sh` | Act 17 corrective cases and Act 27 cycle identity; Act 23 §7 requires original case IDs and evidence preserved | Retained |
+| `government/outcome-metrics.py`, `tests/outcome-metrics-smoke.sh` | Act 18 board reporting, preserved by Act 23 §4 | Retained |
+| `government/branch-bootstrap.sh`, `government/executive-cycle.sh`, `research-frontier-status.py` | Acts 19/30/31 bootstrap and ordinary office continuity; still called by current `boot.sh` | Retained |
+| `tests/host-ci-policy-smoke.sh` | Act 9 interpretation note (Founder clarification 2026-10-16): GitHub-hosted CI must remain enabled; the test is its negative guard | Retained |
+| `tests/act19-office-continuity-smoke.sh`, `appointment-recovery-integration-smoke.sh`, `boot-smoke.sh`, `clerk-liveness-smoke.sh`, `executive-cycle-smoke.sh`, `executive-recovery-timing-smoke.sh`, `summons-smoke.sh`, `seat-liveness-smoke.sh` | Enforcement tests for Acts 15/17/18/19/21/25/27; Act 21 §1 requires the applicable suite green | Retained |
+
+## Enforcement note for statutory reviewers
+
+A new terminal appointment is never merely an ephemeral stderr line: the
+additive launcher `government/agentic-office.sh` writes one individually
+named immutable open-case receipt per appointment under
+`viche-state/office-blockers/cases` and a current-blocker notice to the Clerk
+and Recovery Steward. A successor must reconcile the original effect, the
+Judiciary must independently verify, and no runtime mechanism silently closes
+the record. This candidate does **not** change `boot.sh` or `sitting.sh`
+dispatch behaviour: no office is activated by this commit. Periodic Act 15
+audit omissions themselves remain reportable open findings, not automatically
+inferred healthy states.
